    "media:imagetext": "For A/C\n911CL\n912CL\nONLY\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nCAPITOL\nINTERNATIONAL AIRWAYS\nForm No. G-400\n(Oct. 1, 1978)\nA\n-EXIT\n••0°\nA\nEXIT\nB\nWINDOW EXIT\nA\nEXIT\nDOOR EXIT\nSEAT BELTS\nFASTEN\nPull handle up\nand over. Push\ndoor out.\nUNFASTEN\nKeep seat belt fastened\nwhen seated\nDOOR EXITS AND ESCAPE SLIDES\n2.\nPull Red Handle to\ninflate slide.\n3.\nRemove shoes and\nall sharp objects.\nBRACE POSITION\n4. Jump and sit in slide.\nB.\nPull window handle in\nand down.\nNO SHOES\nESCAPE WINDOWS OVER WINGS\n2.\nRemove shoes\nand all sharp\nobjects.\nDiscard window through\nopening, and exit through\nwindow.\nAt rear of wing.\nslide down flaps.\nNO SHOES\nAUXILIARY DOOR EXITS AND ESCAPE SLIDES\nPull handle in\nand down.\n2.\nLet go of handle when\nexit starts to fall out.\n3.\nRemove shoes and\nall sharp objects.\nJump and sit\nin slide.\nNO SHOES\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE THIS CARD FROM AIRCRAFT",
